  "answer": "The bug is clear: `add` subtracts instead of adding. Let me check the test and package config before fixing.\nFix confirmed needed. The function returns `a - b` instead of `a + b`. Applying the one-line fix, preserving the signature:\nNow running the existing test suite with Bun:\n## Fix summary\n\n**Bug:** `add` in `src/add.ts` performed subtraction — `return a - b` — instead of addition, so every call produced wrong results (e.g. `add(2, 3)` returned `-1` instead of `5`).\n\n**Fix:** One-line change to `return a + b`.\n\n- **Signature preserved:** `export function add(a: number, b: number)` is unchanged.\n- **Tests preserved:** `test/oracle.test.ts` untouched, per AGENTS.md.\n- **Test run:** `bun test` → **1 pass, 0 fail, 5 expect() calls** — all signed-input cases (`2+3`, `-2+3`, `0+0`, `-5+-7`, `99+1`) now pass.\n\nNo other files were modified (`AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and the test file remain byte-identical)."
